# Salmonella enterica serovar Enteritidis, the nine locus MLVA of Malorny et al. 2008, amplified
# in one multiplex reaction. The loci are in the order the Methods give for the MLVA type,
# SENTR7-SENTR5-SENTR6-SENTR2-SENTR3-SENTR4-SE3-SENTR1-SE7, so a profile string reads as the
# published type.
#
# Primers are Table 2 as published. The 5' dye label of each forward primer, FAM, HEX or TET, is
# an assay property and is not part of the oligonucleotide, so it is not written here.
#
# The search window is derived, not published: it runs from the length of the amplicon with no
# repeat to five repeats beyond the largest product Table 3 reports, with that table's capillary
# sizes first corrected to sequence lengths by the per locus offset Table 2 shows.

SENTR7	ACGATCACCACGGTCACTTC	CGGATAACAACAGGACGCTTC	107-181
SENTR5	CACCGCACAATCAGTGGAAC	GCGTTGAATATCGGCAGCATG	211-357
SENTR6	ATGGACGGAGGCGATAGAC	AGCTTCACAATTTGCGTATTCG	144-270
SENTR2	CACTGGACGATCTGGATTTCTC	GTCGCCGTTACGCATCAAC	156-715
SENTR3	CTAAACAAGCCGCTCATCCG	ACAACCTGCTGCTGTGCTG	84-1053
SENTR4	GACCAACACTCTATGAACCAATG	ACCAGGCAACTATTCGCTATC	85-168
SE-3	CAACAAAACAACAGCAGCAT	GGGAAACGGTAATCAGAAAGT	272-381
SENTR1	GCAACAGCAGCAGCAACAG	CCGAGCTGAGATCGCCAAG	89-668
SE-7	GATAATGCTGCCGTTGGTAA	ACTGCGTTTGGTTTCTTTTCT	198-1081
